## Automatic Layouts

To create an automatic layout, add the `@Layout` annotation to a router layout. This layout is automatically applied to all views unless explicitly disabled.

The following example applies `MainLayout` to **all views**:

```java
/ tag::snippet[]
@Layout
/ end::snippet[]
public class MainLayout extends AppLayout { / ①
    ...
}
```
1. `AppLayout` is a built-in router layout. See its [documentation page](/components/app-layout) for more details.

<dl><dt><strong>❗ IMPORTANT: Security Annotations Required</strong></dt><dd>

When view access control is enabled, a `@Layout` class needs its **own** access annotation -- such as `@AnonymousAllowed`, `@PermitAll`, or `@RolesAllowed` -- in addition to the annotations on the views it renders. Annotating only the views isn’t enough: if the layout itself isn’t accessible, navigation to any view inside it is denied with a message such as _"Denied access to view 'DirectoryView' due to layout 'MainLayout' access rules."_

